course: dictionary
lesson: 13186
title: The word fried
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fried is a describing word. Fried food has been cooked in hot oil or fat, like «fried eggs» or «fried rice». You can read fried as an adjective, because it tells you what kind of food it is.
explain: Fried is also the past form of the verb fry. The verb changes: fry, fries, fried, frying. «Sam fries the onions» is happening now, but «Sam fried the onions» means he cooked them earlier. Look for a time in the past, and you can spot the past form.
explain: Careful: fried has an informal meaning too. «After the long test, my brain felt fried» means very tired. «The computer got fried in the storm» means it was broken by too much heat or electricity. Read the words around fried to find out which meaning is right.
fact: Fried food has been cooked in hot oil or fat.
fact: «Fried» is the past form of the verb «fry».
fact: «Fried rice» and «fried chicken» are tasty, but they are best eaten only now and then.
fact: Informal: «fried» can mean very tired, as in «I'm fried after football».
fact: Phrases like «stir-fried» and «deep-fried» use fried to show how the food was cooked.
exercise: «Mum made fried eggs for breakfast.» What does fried mean here? | Boiled in water | Raw and fresh | Frozen and cold | *Cooked in hot oil or fat
exercise: «Yesterday, Sam fried the onions for the stew.» Which word is the past form of fry? | fries | frying | fry | *fried
exercise: «After the long test, my brain felt fried.» What does fried mean here? | *Very tired | Very hot from the sun | Very hungry | Very wet from rain
test: «The old computer got fried when it was left in the sun.» What does fried mean here? | Cleaned and polished | Full of songs | Covered in oil | *Broken by too much heat or electricity
test: Which sentence uses fried as the past form of fry? | «The fried rice was hot and spicy.» | «Fried chicken is my favourite food.» | *«Ali fried two eggs before school.»
exam: «Let's have fried eggs, not boiled ones.» What does fried mean? | *Cooked in hot oil or fat | Cooked in water | Frozen solid | Cold and raw
